// Single source of truth for the bot's public command list — used by both
// the in-chat .menu command (index.js) and README.md's command reference
// tables (regenerated by generate_readme_commands.js), so the two can
// never silently drift apart from each other. If a command changes name,
// gets removed, or its behavior changes, update it HERE and both
// consumers automatically reflect it — never hand-edit a duplicated copy
// in index.js or the README again.
//
// Each section is { emoji, title, items, note? }. `note` is optional —
// a short blurb shown once under the section heading, above its command
// list, for context that applies to the whole section rather than one
// command (e.g. GAMES' "all four support PvP and a bot opponent" line).
// Keep it here rather than hand-writing it into just the README or just
// the .menu output — either of those alone is exactly the kind of
// silent-drift risk this file exists to prevent; see GAMES below for the
// one section currently using it.
//
// AUDITED (Aug 2026): every entry below was checked against the actual
// command implementation, not guessed from the name. Owner-only admin
// tools (card catalogue management like .addcard/.mergecards/.repairlinks,
// the .addxp testing command, etc.) are deliberately left off — this is
// the PUBLIC command list.

